# The lines that pg_dump can write differently for a copy that usql made and
# a copy that pg_dump made. Each line below is a regular expression of Go,
# and a line of either dump that it matches is left out of the comparison.

# dbmeta sets a sequence that a column owns to the largest value of the
# column, and pg_dump to the last value of the sequence. Both give the same
# next value. A sequence that no column owns, such as app.ticket_seq, keeps
# the value it starts with. Reported to dbmeta on 2026-11-08.
^SELECT pg_catalog\.setval\(
